WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.722
The AI features work for the administrator out of the box.

00:00:04.722 --> 00:00:06.932
Everyone else needs permissions.

00:00:06.932 --> 00:00:11.818
This video shows which roles an AI project usually needs, the permissions each

00:00:11.818 --> 00:00:16.238
one gets, and what to check when a feature works for the administrator

00:00:16.238 --> 00:00:17.750
and for nobody else.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.519
Builders create and tune the assistants:

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:29.790
profiles, deployments, knowledge, tools and connections.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.410
Analysts read the reports of the chats, and can export them.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.400
Staff chat with the assistants of their work.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.403
Anonymous visitors only talk to a public assistant.

00:00:41.403 --> 00:00:44.370
Each group is a role with its own permissions.

00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:52.268
Open Access Control, Roles, and click Add Role.

00:00:52.268 --> 00:00:57.145
Give it a name, AI builder, and a description, and click Create.

00:00:57.597 --> 00:00:59.270
Then edit the role.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:02.280
The permissions are grouped by feature.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:09.237
Under AI Services, tick Manage AI profiles, Manage AI deployments and Manage AI profile templates.

00:01:09.707 --> 00:01:12.381
Knowledge has its own permissions:

00:01:12.381 --> 00:01:17.327
Manage AI data sources, Manage file sources and Manage web crawlers.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:20.001
Tools and connections have theirs:

00:01:20.001 --> 00:01:26.217
Manage AI tool instances, Manage MCP Connections and Manage Agent-to-Agent Connections.

00:01:29.326 --> 00:01:34.293
Manage AI Provider Connections lets a person change the connections to your AI

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.481
services, so give it with care.

00:01:36.481 --> 00:01:37.486
Click Save.

00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:45.566
People who chat need permission to talk to a profile.

00:01:45.566 --> 00:01:48.699
Query any AI profile covers every profile.

00:01:48.699 --> 00:01:54.965
For one assistant only, tick Query AI profile for that profile, such as support-assistant.

00:01:55.421 --> 00:02:00.244
Delete chat session lets people delete their own chats, and Delete all chat

00:02:00.244 --> 00:02:02.805
sessions lets them delete everyone's.

00:02:02.805 --> 00:02:06.081
Clear AI memory lets them clear their own memory.

00:02:06.532 --> 00:02:13.232
View AI Chat Analytics opens the AI reports, and Export AI Chat Analytics allows the download.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:18.792
Chat interactions have their own permissions, such as List chat interactions.

00:02:22.993 --> 00:02:24.940
Tools are checked twice.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:30.000
Access any AI tool opens every tool, and it is marked Security Critical.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.672
Below it, each tool has its own Access permission, so you can open

00:02:34.672 --> 00:02:36.813
only the ones a role needs.

00:02:37.263 --> 00:02:40.937
For a public assistant, open the Anonymous role.

00:02:40.937 --> 00:02:44.748
Tick only Query AI profile for the public profile.

00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:50.463
Never give the Anonymous role Access any AI tool, or a way to manage anything.

00:02:54.663 --> 00:02:59.258
The administrator has every permission, so a feature that works only for the

00:02:59.258 --> 00:03:01.723
administrator is a permission problem.

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:04.325
Check the role of the person:

00:03:04.325 --> 00:03:07.765
is the right permission ticked, in the right feature group?

00:03:07.765 --> 00:03:10.993
For a chat, check the Query permission of that profile.

00:03:11.743 --> 00:03:15.784
For a tool, check Access any AI tool or the permission of the

00:03:15.784 --> 00:03:19.403
tool, and for a public chat, check the Anonymous role.

00:03:21.403 --> 00:03:25.314
Create a role for each kind of person, give each only what it

00:03:25.314 --> 00:03:28.525
needs, and keep tools and anonymous access tight.

00:03:28.525 --> 00:03:30.043
Thanks for watching.

